WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.164 --> 00:00:17.288
The caravan entered Istanbul.

2
00:00:18.649 --> 00:00:19.889
The streets were crowded.

3
00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:25.411
Most men wore hats that were shaped like an upside-down flower pot.

4
00:00:26.611 --> 00:00:29.192
Each hat had a silk tail on top of it.

5
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:34.703
Women wore long coats, and some covered their faces with a cloth.

6
00:00:36.264 --> 00:00:40.967
As the caravan passed by, people on the street called out to the travelers.

7
00:00:42.048 --> 00:00:43.729
"What goods have you brought this time?"

8
00:00:43.749 --> 00:00:46.811
"Do you have any Chinese silk?"

9
00:00:46.831 --> 00:00:49.933
"Come to the Grand Bazaar!"

10
00:00:50.514 --> 00:00:52.415
shouted someone from the caravan.

11
00:00:52.435 --> 00:00:55.477
"Then you can see what we have!"

12
00:00:56.858 --> 00:01:00.080
The caravan stopped in front of a beautiful building.

13
00:01:01.148 --> 00:01:04.789
Through the main doorway, Mandy could see stalls and shops.

14
00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:08.770
They were filled with colorful items.

15
00:01:09.991 --> 00:01:13.332
People from the caravan were unloading things to sell.

16
00:01:13.352 --> 00:01:16.893
"Wow! I'd like to shop here!"

17
00:01:17.593 --> 00:01:18.733
exclaimed Mandy.

18
00:01:18.753 --> 00:01:21.654
"What's that in your hand?"

19
00:01:22.294 --> 00:01:22.955
asked Vinnie.

20
00:01:25.135 --> 00:01:27.616
Mandy held up a pair of diamond earrings.

21
00:01:28.944 --> 00:01:32.467
"I forgot—Mom asked me to put these in her drawer!"

22
00:01:33.148 --> 00:01:33.828
she cried.

23
00:01:33.848 --> 00:01:38.392
"You'd better not lose them," warned Vinnie.

24
00:01:38.412 --> 00:01:41.074
"She'll be really upset."

25
00:01:43.276 --> 00:01:45.798
Mandy shrugged and put them in her pocket.

26
00:01:45.818 --> 00:01:48.981
"They're not real diamonds anyway."

27
00:01:49.001 --> 00:01:52.464
"How do we get off this animal?"

28
00:01:53.024 --> 00:01:54.705
said Vinnie, looking down.

29
00:01:55.846 --> 00:01:57.468
The camel stood quietly.

30
00:01:58.508 --> 00:02:01.510
"Maybe we can jump," suggested Mandy.

31
00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:07.775
"If you jump, you will break your leg or your neck," a man's voice said from below.

32
00:02:08.955 --> 00:02:11.817
Vinnie and Mandy saw a man staring at them.

33
00:02:11.837 --> 00:02:14.159
"How did you get up there?"

34
00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.781
the man asked, petting the camel.

35
00:02:16.801 --> 00:02:20.944
"Kiraz the camel was not carrying any people earlier."

36
00:02:20.964 --> 00:02:26.568
"Uh, well, we Vinnie tried to explain.

37
00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:32.230
The man spoke to the camel and Kiraz knelt down.

38
00:02:33.591 --> 00:02:35.452
The children climbed off his back.

39
00:02:35.472 --> 00:02:38.734
"Thank you, sir," said Mandy.

40
00:02:38.754 --> 00:02:40.435
"Who are you?"

41
00:02:40.895 --> 00:02:41.676
the man asked.

42
00:02:43.076 --> 00:02:45.118
The children introduced themselves.

43
00:02:45.138 --> 00:02:48.199
"I am Ali," said the man.

44
00:02:48.219 --> 00:02:51.041
"I sell carpets and other things."

45
00:02:52.462 --> 00:02:55.904
The camel opened his mouth and stuck out a gray tongue.

46
00:02:57.068 --> 00:02:59.770
"I think Kiraz likes you!"

47
00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:01.030
laughed Ali.

48
00:03:02.331 --> 00:03:06.753
Vinnie and Mandy helped Ali carry rolls of carpets into the building.

49
00:03:06.773 --> 00:03:11.976
"The Grand Bazaar is the biggest market in the world," Ali explained.

50
00:03:11.996 --> 00:03:15.158
"It is one of the best places to buy and sell."

51
00:03:16.919 --> 00:03:19.460
"It's amazing," Mandy remarked.

52
00:03:20.161 --> 00:03:21.681
"It looks like the mall!"

53
00:03:23.262 --> 00:03:26.344
Many shops lined each side of the long building.

54
00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:31.261
People strolled down the middle, looking and buying.

55
00:03:32.201 --> 00:03:34.342
Ali stopped in front of one shop.

56
00:03:35.442 --> 00:03:37.823
A woman and a boy were already there.

57
00:03:38.823 --> 00:03:42.364
They were setting out beautiful pieces of jewelry and dishes.

58
00:03:42.384 --> 00:03:46.105
"This is my family," Ali said.

59
00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:49.786
"As you see, we sell many things, including carpets!"

60
00:03:51.007 --> 00:03:52.227
He turned to his son.

61
00:03:52.247 --> 00:03:54.968
"Berk, take this bag to the coffee shop.

62
00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:58.223
Ask Hasad the owner to exchange it for silver."

63
00:03:59.164 --> 00:04:00.085
The boy nodded.

64
00:04:00.105 --> 00:04:02.207
"Can we go too?"

65
00:04:02.787 --> 00:04:03.448
asked Vinnie.

66
00:04:04.709 --> 00:04:06.211
Berk looked at his father.

67
00:04:06.231 --> 00:04:11.517
"Sure! The coffee shop is always fun to visit," Ali said.

68
00:04:11.537 --> 00:04:13.759
"But don't stay too long."
